WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.104
The need for

00:00:00.916 --> 00:00:02.484
a formally verifiable

00:00:02.296 --> 00:00:03.758
mainstream programming

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:04.300
language

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:05.903
An argument that

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:07.094
mainstream programming

00:00:06.905 --> 00:00:07.884
needs a language

00:00:07.696 --> 00:00:09.039
designed for formal

00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:10.148
verification from the

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:10.608
start

00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:12.560
Because of LLMs

00:00:12.691 --> 00:00:13.598
the discipline of

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.825
software engineering

00:00:14.648 --> 00:00:15.768
is in crisis

00:00:15.907 --> 00:00:17.416
Quality is nose-diving

00:00:17.511 --> 00:00:18.194
and I see

00:00:18.006 --> 00:00:18.973
no reason why

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:19.468
it won't keep

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.187
getting worse

00:00:20.726 --> 00:00:21.846
My chosen angle

00:00:21.658 --> 00:00:22.624
is Magmide

00:00:22.766 --> 00:00:23.744
a project whose

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.322
goal is to

00:00:24.134 --> 00:00:25.053
create a new

00:00:24.865 --> 00:00:26.303
formally verifiable

00:00:26.115 --> 00:00:27.259
programming language

00:00:27.318 --> 00:00:28.603
intended for immediate

00:00:28.415 --> 00:00:30.136
adoption by practitioners

00:00:30.654 --> 00:00:31.668
Full story on

00:00:31.479 --> 00:00:32.375
the dashboard
